    {
     "id": "95d0691",
     "elType": "widget",
     "widgetType": "heading",
     "settings": {
      "title": "What does verified mean on this page?",
      "header_size": "h2",
      "_css_classes": "gt-h2"
     },
     "elements": []
    },
    {
     "id": "0bf3f5f",
     "elType": "widget",
     "widgetType": "text-editor",
     "settings": {
      "editor": "<p>Verified means a person at Gototherapy has checked the therapist's entry on their professional register, seen a current insurance certificate, confirmed their supervision arrangement with the supervisor, and matched their identity to the register entry. It is repeated every year. It is not a recommendation and it says nothing about whether a therapist is right for you.</p><p>Roles are checked differently. A coach in the UK has no register, so the coach badge says what was checked and the profile says plainly that there is no register. <a href=\"/how-we-verify/\">How we verify, role by role</a>.</p>",
      "_css_classes": "gt-prose"
     },
     "elements": []
    }
   ],
